    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0347" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg297"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Young.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No: 76.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith for your information
                    copy of a letter from the president of the Pacific Mail Steamship Company, and
                    copy of the Department’s reply thereto, in relation to the firing upon the
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Costa Rica</hi> in the port of Amapala,
                    Honduras, and the position of commanders of merchant vessels as regards demands
                    for the surrender of criminals.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
